14. Interview Important Points

Binary Tree is a non-linear data structure.
Maximum children per node is two.
Inorder traversal of BST gives sorted order.
Skewed tree gives worst case performance.
Complete Binary Tree is used in Heap.

15. When to Use Binary Tree?

When hierarchical data representation is required.
When parent-child relationship exists.
When recursive solutions are efficient.

